{"content_hash": "fa5b5bbf25c0a515", "version_id": 754, "article_id": 76, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Meta offers Zuckerberg new shares to help pay possible wealth tax", "title_zh": "Meta给扎克伯格发新股，帮他应对可能的富豪税", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/22/meta-mark-zuckerberg-california-wealth-tax", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689439518196-f48a24b49fb5?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8bWV0YSUyMHN0cmlrZXMlMjBkZWFsfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTI3OTk4NTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Julio Lopez on Unsplash", "author": "Julio Lopez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@juliolopez?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-person-holding-up-a-cell-phone-in-front-of-a-sign-ilbjfRwOgzA?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(112, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(150, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "ba10886f1e8e"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-24", "word_count": 268, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Meta has made a deal with its chief executive, Mark Zuckerberg, to help him pay a possible new tax on billionaires in California. In return, he has promised to keep living in the state for eight years.", "lead_zh": "Meta与首席执行官马克·扎克伯格达成协议，帮他应对加州可能开征的富豪税。作为交换，他承诺未来八年继续住在加州。", "preview": "The company behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp said the arrangement would keep Zuckerberg in California, where Meta has its headquarter", "preview_zh": "旗下拥有 Facebook、Instagram 和 WhatsApp 的 Meta 表示，这项安排能让扎克伯格留在加州，公司总部就在那里。根据协议，如果加州通过一次性富豪税，他将获得可以出售的新股份，用来支付数十亿美元的税单。作为交换，他同意未来八年继续住在加州，或住在 Meta", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 742, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 104.225, "size_bytes": 626256, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b2_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 106.675, "size_bytes": 640944, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b2_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b2_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 112.7, "size_bytes": 677088, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b2_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b2_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 98.775, "size_bytes": 593568, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b2_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/76/en_b2_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 104.725, "size_bytes": 629280, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 317, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/76/en_b2_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@d92c8fa/content/data/versions/754.json", "paragraphs": ["The company behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp said the arrangement would keep Zuckerberg in California, where Meta has its headquarters. Under the deal, he will receive new shares that could be sold to pay a multibillion-dollar tax bill if California passes a one-off billionaire tax. In exchange, he has agreed to remain a resident of the state, or wherever Meta is based, for eight years.", "Californians will vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires who live in the state. Zuckerberg, who is worth $239bn according to Forbes, told Meta he was thinking about moving his main home elsewhere, because the tax could force him to sell voting shares. Meta is therefore creating a new class of non-voting shares through a two-for-one stock split, so he can sell some without losing control of the company.", "Recent polling shows that Prop 40 still lacks majority support. Several tech billionaires, including Sergey Brin, Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt, have spent heavily to fight the measure. Congressman Rohit Khanna described the vote as a choice between standing with the working class or with the oligarchs. \"Every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay,\" he wrote in the Guardian.", "Meta also reported a 26% rise in quarterly revenues to $64.6bn, beating expectations. However, profits fell by 37% to $13bn, pulled down by a $9.9bn charge linked to lawsuits over child protection and social media addiction. Its shares dropped more than 6% on Thursday, and a New Mexico judge ordered the company to pay $25bn for misleading the public about user data."], "paragraphs_zh": ["旗下拥有 Facebook、Instagram 和 WhatsApp 的 Meta 表示，这项安排能让扎克伯格留在加州，公司总部就在那里。根据协议，如果加州通过一次性富豪税，他将获得可以出售的新股份，用来支付数十亿美元的税单。作为交换，他同意未来八年继续住在加州，或住在 Meta 总部所在地。", "加州选民下月初将就第40号提案投票，该提案对居住在该州的大约250名亿万富翁征收一次性5%的税。据《福布斯》估计身家2390亿美元的扎克伯格告诉 Meta，他正考虑把主要住所搬到别处，因为这项税可能迫使他出售有投票权的股份。因此，Meta 通过二比一的股票拆分，创建了一种新的无投票权股份，让他可以卖掉一部分而不失去对公司的控制。", "近期民调显示，第40号提案仍未获得多数支持。包括谢尔盖·布林、彼得·蒂尔和埃里克·施密特在内的多位科技亿万富翁已投入巨资反对该措施。国会议员罗希特·坎纳把这次投票描述为在站在工人阶级一边还是站在寡头一边之间做选择。他在《卫报》上写道：“每个社会都要征税，唯一的问题是谁来付。”", "Meta 还公布季度营收增长26%，达到646亿美元，超出预期。但利润下降37%，至130亿美元，受到与儿童保护和社交媒体成瘾诉讼相关的99亿美元费用的拖累。其股价周四下跌超过6%，新墨西哥州一名法官还命令该公司支付250亿美元，原因是它在用户数据处理上误导公众。Meta 还表示，员工人数已减至66,775人，比一年前少15%。"], "body": "The company behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp said the arrangement would keep Zuckerberg in California, where Meta has its headquarters. Under the deal, he will receive new shares that could be sold to pay a multibillion-dollar tax bill if California passes a one-off billionaire tax. In exchange, he has agreed to remain a resident of the state, or wherever Meta is based, for eight years.\n\nCalifornians will vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires who live in the state. Zuckerberg, who is worth $239bn according to Forbes, told Meta he was thinking about moving his main home elsewhere, because the tax could force him to sell voting shares. Meta is therefore creating a new class of non-voting shares through a two-for-one stock split, so he can sell some without losing control of the company.\n\nRecent polling shows that Prop 40 still lacks majority support. Several tech billionaires, including Sergey Brin, Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt, have spent heavily to fight the measure. Congressman Rohit Khanna described the vote as a choice between standing with the working class or with the oligarchs. \"Every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay,\" he wrote in the Guardian.\n\nMeta also reported a 26% rise in quarterly revenues to $64.6bn, beating expectations. However, profits fell by 37% to $13bn, pulled down by a $9.9bn charge linked to lawsuits over child protection and social media addiction. Its shares dropped more than 6% on Thursday, and a New Mexico judge ordered the company to pay $25bn for misleading the public about user data.", "body_zh": "旗下拥有 Facebook、Instagram 和 WhatsApp 的 Meta 表示，这项安排能让扎克伯格留在加州，公司总部就在那里。根据协议，如果加州通过一次性富豪税，他将获得可以出售的新股份，用来支付数十亿美元的税单。作为交换，他同意未来八年继续住在加州，或住在 Meta 总部所在地。\n\n加州选民下月初将就第40号提案投票，该提案对居住在该州的大约250名亿万富翁征收一次性5%的税。据《福布斯》估计身家2390亿美元的扎克伯格告诉 Meta，他正考虑把主要住所搬到别处，因为这项税可能迫使他出售有投票权的股份。因此，Meta 通过二比一的股票拆分，创建了一种新的无投票权股份，让他可以卖掉一部分而不失去对公司的控制。\n\n近期民调显示，第40号提案仍未获得多数支持。包括谢尔盖·布林、彼得·蒂尔和埃里克·施密特在内的多位科技亿万富翁已投入巨资反对该措施。国会议员罗希特·坎纳把这次投票描述为在站在工人阶级一边还是站在寡头一边之间做选择。他在《卫报》上写道：“每个社会都要征税，唯一的问题是谁来付。”\n\nMeta 还公布季度营收增长26%，达到646亿美元，超出预期。但利润下降37%，至130亿美元，受到与儿童保护和社交媒体成瘾诉讼相关的99亿美元费用的拖累。其股价周四下跌超过6%，新墨西哥州一名法官还命令该公司支付250亿美元，原因是它在用户数据处理上误导公众。Meta 还表示，员工人数已减至66,775人，比一年前少15%。", "text": "The company behind Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp said the arrangement would keep Zuckerberg in California, where Meta has its headquarters. Under the deal, he will receive new shares that could be sold to pay a multibillion-dollar tax bill if California passes a one-off billionaire tax. In exchange, he has agreed to remain a resident of the state, or wherever Meta is based, for eight years. Californians will vote early next month on Proposition 40, a one-off 5% tax on the roughly 250 billionaires who live in the state. Zuckerberg, who is worth $239bn according to Forbes, told Meta he was thinking about moving his main home elsewhere, because the tax could force him to sell voting shares. Meta is therefore creating a new class of non-voting shares through a two-for-one stock split, so he can sell some without losing control of the company. Recent polling shows that Prop 40 still lacks majority support. Several tech billionaires, including Sergey Brin, Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt, have spent heavily to fight the measure. Congressman Rohit Khanna described the vote as a choice between standing with the working class or with the oligarchs. \"Every society is taxed. The only question is who will pay,\" he wrote in the Guardian. Meta also reported a 26% rise in quarterly revenues to $64.6bn, beating expectations. However, profits fell by 37% to $13bn, pulled down by a $9.9bn charge linked to lawsuits over child protection and social media addiction. Its shares dropped more than 6% on Thursday, and a New Mexico judge ordered the company to pay $25bn for misleading the public about user data.", "vocab": [{"word": "strike a deal", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "达成协议", "note": "常用搭配，比 make a deal 更正式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "chief executive", "pos": "noun", "zh": "首席执行官", "note": "常缩写为 CEO", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "headquarters", "pos": "noun", "zh": "总部", "note": "单复数同形", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "one-off", "pos": "adj", "zh": "一次性的", "note": "英式用法，指只发生一次", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "wealth tax", "pos": "noun", "zh": "财富税、富豪税", "note": "针对资产而非收入征税", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "resident", "pos": "noun", "zh": "居民", "note": "be a resident of 表示居住在", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "stock split", "pos": "noun", "zh": "股票拆分", "note": "金融术语", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "non-voting shares", "pos": "noun", "zh": "无投票权股份", "note": "股东没有表决权", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "polling", "pos": "noun", "zh": "民调", "note": "常用复数 polls", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "measure", "pos": "noun", "zh": "措施、议案", "note": "政治语境中指待表决的提案", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "revenue", "pos": "noun", "zh": "营收、收入", "note": "公司财务常用词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "headcount", "pos": "noun", "zh": "员工人数", "note": "人力资源用语", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-10-23T23:57:30.310630", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.25, "e": 0.325, "sm": 250, "em": 325, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "company", "s": 0.325, "e": 0.725, "sm": 325, "em": 724, "cs": 4, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "behind", "s": 0.725, "e": 1.125, "sm": 725, "em": 1125, "cs": 12, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "Facebook", "s": 1.125, "e": 1.825, "sm": 1125, "em": 1825, "cs": 19, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": ",", "s": 1.825, "e": 1.925, "sm": 1825, "em": 1925, "cs": 27, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Instagram", "s": 1.925, "e": 2.6, "sm": 1925, "em": 2600, "cs": 29, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "and", "s": 2.6, "e": 2.725, "sm": 2600, "em": 2725, "cs": 39, "ce": 42, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "WhatsApp", "s": 2.725, "e": 3.5, "sm": 2725, "em": 3499, "cs": 43, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "said", "s": 3.5, "e": 3.688, "sm": 3500, "em": 3687, "cs": 52, "ce": 56, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "the", "s": 3.688, "e": 3.8, "sm": 3687, "em": 3799, "cs": 57, "ce": 60, "si": 0}, {